  "id": "BIT-sqlite-2026-119379",
  "summary": "SQLite before 3.54.0 Heap Buffer Overflow via Session Extension sessionUpdateFind()",
  "details": "SQLite before 3.54.0 built with the session extension contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in sqlite3changeset_apply() that allows attackers to corrupt heap memory by supplying crafted changesets. Attackers can repeat a table name in a second changeset block with a larger column count, causing sessionUpdateFind() to memset past the undersized aUpdateMask allocation.",
